      },
      {
        "id": "sh/0ni1w7q1",
        "kind": "textbox",
        "text": "Introduction\n",
        "position": {
          "left": 63.99,
          "top": 28.65,
          "width": 1152,
          "height": 120.19
        },
        "style": {
          "fontSize": 64,
          "typeface": "Times New Roman",
          "color": "#FF0000",
          "alignment": "center"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "sh/fm90n29w",
        "kind": "textbox",
        "text": "What is the project about? CampusNLP is an intelligent NLP system designed to understand student queries, predict their intent, retrieve relevant academic evidence from an institutional knowledge base, and produce a grounded response with source citations.\nApplication domain: Natural Language Processing and Information Retrieval applied to university student services (e.g., academic regulations, curriculum, attendance rules).\nWhy is this topic important? Students often struggle to find accurate, institution-specific answers quickly. A grounded NLP system provides instant, reliable answers without fabricating information (hallucinations).\nWhat motivated the team? We wanted to build a practical, hybrid NLP pipeline that goes beyond a simple LLM chatbot by combining intent classification and semantic retrieval, and crucially, knows how to abstain when reliable evidence is unavailable.",
        "position": {
          "left": 66.33,
          "top": 132.17,
          "width": 1152,
          "height": 523.84
        },
        "style": {
          "fontSize": 26.67,
          "typeface": "Times New Roman",
          "color": "#000000",
          "bold": true,
          "alignment": "left"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
