        }
      },
      {
        "id": "sh/9o76lkzq",
        "kind": "textbox",
        "text": "Problem Definition",
        "position": {
          "left": 63.99,
          "top": 28.65,
          "width": 1152,
          "height": 120.19
        },
        "style": {
          "fontSize": 64,
          "typeface": "Times New Roman",
          "color": "#FF0000",
          "alignment": "center"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "sh/ri58ba1c",
        "kind": "textbox",
        "text": "Existing problem: Institutional knowledge is scattered across various documents (regulations, curriculum, hostel rules), making manual search inefficient and time-consuming.\nDifficulties faced: Students face delays in getting answers. Plain keyword searches fail on complexly worded queries, and off-the-shelf LLMs often invent incorrect, unverified answers.\nWhy the problem is important: Misinformation or delays can negatively affect a student’s academic planning, course registration, and compliance with university rules.\nWho is affected: University students, faculty, and administrative staff who handle repetitive queries.\nWhat needs to be improved: A system that understands natural-language questions, directly extracts exact evidence from official documents, and only answers when highly confident.",
        "position": {
          "left": 62.67,
          "top": 148.84,
          "width": 1152,
          "height": 523.84
        },
        "style": {
          "fontSize": 26.67,
          "typeface": "Times New Roman",
          "color": "#000000",
          "bold": true,
          "alignment": "left"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
