      {
        "id": "sh/rytgzu98",
        "kind": "textbox",
        "text": "Modules",
        "position": {
          "left": 63.99,
          "top": 28.61,
          "width": 1152,
          "height": 91.35
        },
        "style": {
          "fontSize": 64,
          "typeface": "Times New Roman",
          "color": "#FF0000",
          "alignment": "center"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "sh/sz2xszad",
        "kind": "textbox",
        "text": "NLP Text Preprocessing & Feature Extraction\nTransforms raw natural language into machine-readable formats. Employs advanced tokenization, noise reduction, and TF-IDF (Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency) vectorization.\nMachine Learning Intent Classification\nA dedicated ML module that learns from 50,000 query examples (CampusFAQ-50K). It uses classification algorithms to categorize queries across 24 intent classes with high F1-score accuracy.\nSemantic Embedding & Document Retrieval\nConverts institutional text chunks into dense multidimensional vector embeddings. The retrieval module performs rapid similarity searches across this vector space to fetch exact evidence while preserving source metadata.",
        "position": {
          "left": 66.33,
          "top": 132.13,
          "width": 1152,
          "height": 523.84
        },
        "style": {
          "fontSize": 26.67,
          "typeface": "Times New Roman",
          "color": "#FF0000",
          "alignment": "left"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
