      {
        "id": "sh/byh8fm5w",
        "kind": "textbox",
        "text": "Core NLP & ML Algorithms",
        "position": {
          "left": 63.99,
          "top": 28.61,
          "width": 1152,
          "height": 91.35
        },
        "style": {
          "fontSize": 64,
          "typeface": "Times New Roman",
          "color": "#FF0000",
          "alignment": "center"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "sh/cjqpormh",
        "kind": "textbox",
        "text": "Intent Classification Models (TF-IDF + LR/SVM)\nTF-IDF Vectorization: Weights terms by their frequency in a query vs. their rarity across the dataset.\nLogistic Regression & Linear SVM: These algorithms learn the decision boundaries between 24 intents, providing highly accurate and fast structured query routing.\nSemantic Retrieval Models (Embeddings & Cosine Similarity)\nDense Vector Embeddings: Encodes the semantic meaning of sentences into numerical vectors, allowing the system to match paraphrased questions even if exact keywords differ.\nCosine Similarity: Ranks passages by measuring the cosine of the angle between the query vector and document chunk vectors: cos(θ) = (A · B) / (||A|| ||B||).\nAlgorithmic Thresholding (The \"Abstention\" Logic)\nApplies a strict mathematical confidence threshold to the similarity scores. If the highest score falls below the threshold, the system deterministically abstains, ensuring zero hallucinations.",
        "position": {
          "left": 66.33,
          "top": 132.13,
          "width": 1152,
          "height": 523.84
        },
        "style": {
          "fontSize": 26.67,
          "typeface": "Times New Roman",
          "color": "#FF0000",
          "alignment": "left"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
